  "notes": {
    "fs1": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "page": "final",
      "text": "Home holds every lead and draft. Each case runs Brief, Matches, Evidence map, Pitch. Archives sits next to Home in the top bar. Press Play on Home to click through.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 0
    },
    "fs3": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "page": "final",
      "text": "PDF and website input with used, ignored and struck passages. The states around the happy path. Mutz open with sourced answers and confirm buttons. After sending: timeline, re-evaluate, pitch v2, then intro drafts and the visit day.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 2680
    },
    "fs4": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "page": "final",
      "text": "Why not X makes the ranking inspectable. Pipeline is a second view of Leads. Every triaged lead leaves an anonymous trace that feeds the gap report and the capability map under Insights.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 4140
    },
    "ft4": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 5360,
      "page": "final",
      "text": "Final flow: inspectable ranking, pipeline, learning",
      "w": 240,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 3860
    },
    "ft1": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 5360,
      "page": "final",
      "text": "Final flow: from lead to evidence",
      "w": 240,
      "x": 0,
      "y": -280
    },
    "ft2": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 5360,
      "page": "final",
      "text": "Final flow: pitch, export, archives, evaluation",
      "w": 240,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 1060
    },
    "ft3": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 6720,
      "page": "final",
      "text": "Final flow: inputs, states, Mutz, after sending",
      "w": 240,
      "x": 0,
      "y": 2400
    },
    "s1": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "The playbook baseline. A stepper across the top, one job per screen. Mutz floats on every screen. Safest to build tonight.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 0
    },
    "s10": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "Matches are ranked with industry openness signals, then dropped into a draft meeting schedule. The teaser ends with the proposed day.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 12060
    },
    "s2": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "No page changes. Three columns that fill left to right as the officer works. The four frames are states of the same screen.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 1340
    },
    "s3": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "The brief instantly becomes an A4 draft with empty slots. Each slot asks for evidence and opens a drawer of candidates. Matches only exist in service of a sentence.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 2680
    },
    "s4": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "Kanban by need. Accepting moves a row into the Pitch column. Coverage pots sit in each column header, so weak needs are obvious before writing.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 4020
    },
    "s5": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "The left to right tree is the main navigation. Read, Derived, Assumed and Missing edges make trust visible. Clicking a sentence in the A4 lights its path.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 5360
    },
    "s6": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "Built around the officer's queue, not a single search. Each S-GE lead gets a status, a bid decision, triage and a sent version history.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 6700
    },
    "s7": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "Like the last winner's single item tree. One match fills the screen with its provenance tree and detail strip. A to accept, R to reject, S to skip.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 8040
    },
    "s8": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "For the officer who wants density. Facets, sorting, side by side compare, and the Archives page that proves new sites come from config.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 9380
    },
    "s9": {
      "fill": "gray",
      "text": "We cannot oversell. The first answer is a needs by archive matrix of honey pots. Only strong needs go forward; weak leads get an honest decline note.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": -460,
      "y": 10720
    },
    "t1": {
      "kind": "title1",
      "maxW": 5360,
